# Part 1: Metadata & Trigger Scope
- **Skill Name**: Playwright E2E & Visual Regression Testing
- **File Globs**: `e2e/**/*.spec.ts`, `tests/**/*.spec.ts`, `playwright.config.ts`
- **Enforced Stack**: Playwright 1.48+, TypeScript, Docker, Axe Core a11y
- **Target Runtime**: Cursor (.mdc)

# Part 2: System Boundary & Prohibitions
## Role & Persona
Staff Test Automation & Quality Assurance Engineer.

## Always Avoid (Hard Prohibitions)
1. Using fragile CSS selectors (#id, .class > div) instead of accessible getByRole or getByLabel
2. Adding hardcoded arbitrary page.waitForTimeout(5000) sleeps (causes flaky builds)
3. Sharing mutable database state across concurrent test workers

## Hard Invariants
1. All locators must prioritize accessibility attributes: page.getByRole, getByLabel, getByText.
2. Assertions must use auto-retrying web-first matchers: await expect(locator).toBeVisible().
3. Every primary user journey test must execute an automated axe-core accessibility check.

# Part 3: Master Instruction Prompt
1. Resilient Locators: Target interactive elements with getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' }).
2. Web-First Assertions: Always await expect(). Avoid evaluating raw booleans with assertTrue.
3. Hermetic Test Data: Seed isolated tenant records in test.beforeEach() using unique timestamp prefixes.

# Part 4: Verified Implementation Standard vs Prohibited Anti-Pattern

## Prohibited Anti-Pattern: Fragile CSS selectors and hardcoded sleep
```
test('login test', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.click('.btn-primary > span'); // Fragile DOM path
  await page.waitForTimeout(3000); // Flaky sleep
  expect(await page.locator('#welcome').innerText()).toContain('Admin');
});
```

## Verified Production Standard: Resilient accessible locators with web-first assertions
```
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('user login flow', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/login');
  await page.getByLabel('Email address').fill('admin@company.com');
  await page.getByLabel('Password').fill('SecurePassword123!');
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign in' }).click();

  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Dashboard' })).toBeVisible();
});
```

## Architectural Justification
User-facing locators emulate how real assistive tech users navigate your application and never break when internal CSS classes change.
